    <briefdescription>
<para>Exception signalling that the connection pool could not lease a connection in time. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Distinguishes pool exhaustion from a genuine query failure so the HTTP layer can map it to 503 (<ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref> Unavailable) with Retry-After rather than 500. Derives from <computeroutput>std::runtime_error</computeroutput> so generic handlers still catch it. <simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Http_1aaddeb034a51d7050d6cc65cc2b46fdcf" kindref="member">api::v2::Http::statusForException</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a39716826b3e5be2f15603d8cf809446b" kindref="member">DatabaseConnectionPool::get_connection</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
